      "releaseVersionId": "version-macos-26-7",
      "authorship": "originalSynthesis",
      "overview": {
        "authorship": "originalSynthesis",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "macOS Tahoe 26.7 entered release-candidate testing on August 17, 2026 as build 25G220, followed one week later by RC 2 build 25G224. Neither appearance was a public release, and Apple had not added 26.7 to its security-release index as of August 29.",
            "citations": [
              {"url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/17/apple-rolls-out-release-candidates-for-macos-tahoe-26-7-and-macos-sequoia-15-8/", "locator": "macOS Tahoe 26.7 release candidate, build 25G220, August 17, 2026"},
              {"url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/24/second-release-candidates-for-macos-tahoe-26-7-and-macos-sequoia-15-8-now-available/", "locator": "macOS Tahoe 26.7 RC 2, build 25G224, August 24, 2026"},
              {"url": "https://support.apple.com/en-us/100100", "locator": "Apple security releases table reviewed August 29, 2026; no macOS Tahoe 26.7 public row"}
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The first candidate became notable because reporters inspecting the distributed build found references and assets for unannounced hardware, including a demonstration video associated with camera-equipped AirPods. Those artifacts establish what was present in the build; they do not confirm a product name, launch date, or commercial release.",
            "citations": [
              {"url": "https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/17/macos-26-7-unreleased-apple-devices/", "locator": "Article body listing unreleased product references found in macOS Tahoe 26.7 RC"},
              {"url": "https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/17/camera-equipped-airpods-macos-26-7/", "locator": "Article body describing the AirPods demonstration video and B790 code string found in the RC"}
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
