    {
      "target": {"stableEventId": "event:apple:macos:26.7:rc"},
      "authorship": "originalSynthesis",
      "summary": "Apple seeded macOS Tahoe 26.7 RC build 25G220 on August 17, 2026. Reporting based on inspection of the distributed build found references and assets for unannounced hardware, including a camera-equipped AirPods demonstration video. Version Record records those artifacts without treating them as confirmation of future products or release timing.",
      "article": {
        "authorship": "originalSynthesis",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Apple seeded the first macOS Tahoe 26.7 release candidate on August 17, 2026 as build 25G220. The candidate arrived alongside macOS Sequoia 15.8 RC, outside Apple's rolling developer releases feed.",
            "citations": [
              {"url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/17/apple-rolls-out-release-candidates-for-macos-tahoe-26-7-and-macos-sequoia-15-8/", "locator": "macOS Tahoe 26.7 release candidate, build 25G220, August 17, 2026"},
              {"url": "https://developer.apple.com/news/releases/", "locator": "Releases feed reviewed for August 17, 2026 entries"}
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The build drew attention for what reporters found inside it. MacRumors documented references to more than ten unannounced products, while a separate inspection found a demonstration video and code string associated with camera-equipped AirPods identified as B790.",
            "citations": [
              {"url": "https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/17/macos-26-7-unreleased-apple-devices/", "locator": "Article body enumerating unreleased product references in the RC"},
              {"url": "https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/17/camera-equipped-airpods-macos-26-7/", "locator": "Article body describing the demonstration video and B790 image-stream string"}
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A later MacRumors analysis relayed the view that an internal development branch was likely merged into the shipping branch by mistake. Apple has not published that explanation. The archive therefore separates the observed artifacts from the reported explanation and from any prediction about what Apple will sell.",
            "citations": [
              {"url": "https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/24/how-apple-leaked-itself/", "locator": "Article discussion of the likely internal-branch merge explanation and its attribution"},
              {"url": "https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/17/camera-equipped-airpods-macos-26-7/", "locator": "Reported build contents"}
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "citations": [
        {"url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/17/apple-rolls-out-release-candidates-for-macos-tahoe-26-7-and-macos-sequoia-15-8/", "locator": "macOS Tahoe 26.7 RC, build 25G220"},
        {"url": "https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/17/camera-equipped-airpods-macos-26-7/", "locator": "Camera-equipped AirPods video and B790 code string found in the RC"}
      ],
      "provenanceStatus": "editoriallyVerified",
      "editorialReview": {"status": "approved", "reviewedAt": "2026-08-29T16:00:00Z"},
      "isIndexable": true
    },
    {
