      "authorship": "originalSynthesis",
      "summary": "Apple seeded macOS Tahoe 26.7 RC 2 on August 24, 2026 as build 25G224, seven days after build 25G220. One outlet reports that the second candidate removed the unannounced-product references and media found in RC 1. Apple has not documented that cleanup, and Version Record records it as reported rather than confirmed.",
      "article": {
        "authorship": "originalSynthesis",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "macOS Tahoe 26.7 RC 2 arrived on August 24, 2026 as build 25G224, one week after RC build 25G220. The numeric part of the build advanced by four, matching the movement from 24H16 to 24H20 in the macOS Sequoia 15.8 candidate released beside it.",
            "citations": [
              {"url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/24/second-release-candidates-for-macos-tahoe-26-7-and-macos-sequoia-15-8-now-available/", "locator": "RC 2 build numbers 25G224 and 24H20; one week after the first candidates"},
              {"url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/17/apple-rolls-out-release-candidates-for-macos-tahoe-26-7-and-macos-sequoia-15-8/", "locator": "First-candidate build numbers 25G220 and 24H16"}
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The second candidate followed the unusually broad leak in RC 1, where reporters found unannounced-device references and a camera-equipped AirPods demonstration video. Tech Times reports that RC 2 removed those references, media assets, and staging code.",
            "citations": [
              {"url": "https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/17/camera-equipped-airpods-macos-26-7/", "locator": "AirPods demonstration video and B790 code string found in RC 1"},
              {"url": "https://www.techtimes.com/articles/325521/20260825/apple-erases-its-own-leak-macos-267-rc2-scrubs-foldable-iphone-camera-airpods-code.htm", "locator": "Article reporting that RC 2 removed internal hardware references, media assets, and staging code"}
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Apple has not published a change note confirming that cleanup, and Version Record has not independently compared the two binaries. The removal is therefore an attributed report, not a confirmed Apple changelog item. The existence of artifacts in RC 1 also remains separate from whether any referenced product will ship.",
            "citations": [
              {"url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/24/second-release-candidates-for-macos-tahoe-26-7-and-macos-sequoia-15-8-now-available/", "locator": "RC 2 release report listing builds without an Apple cleanup note"},
              {"url": "https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/24/how-apple-leaked-itself/", "locator": "Analysis distinguishing build artifacts, reported explanation, and expected cleanup"}
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
